.TH RETRY 1 "October 2023" "retry" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
retry \- the missing retry command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B retry
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B retry
automatically re-runs a shell command until it succeeds or the configured
maximum number of attempts is reached. The command is executed via
.BR "bash -c" ,
so shell features such as pipelines and environment expansion are available.
.PP
Options must appear before the command to run. Use
.B \-\-
to terminate option parsing when the wrapped command accepts its own flags.
.PP
On every invocation the command's standard input, output, and environment are
the same as
.B retry
unless otherwise redirected. Command output is printed after a successful run.
When
.B \-\-verbose
is enabled, the command's output from every attempt is streamed and
informational messages of the form "retrying N of M" are written to standard
error. If all attempts fail a final diagnostic message is printed before
.B retry
exits with status 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c , \-\-count " " \fIn\fR
Number of attempts to make. The default is 5.
.TP
.BR \-i , \-\-interval " " \fIduration\fR
Time to wait between attempts. The default is 3s.
.TP
.BR \-t , \-\-timeout " " \fIduration\fR
Maximum running time allowed for each individual attempt. The default is 1s.
When the timeout expires the running command is terminated and the next
attempt begins after the configured interval.
.TP
.BR \-v , \-\-verbose
Print progress messages before every attempt and stream the command's output
for each retry. Without this flag the output from failed attempts is
suppressed until the final try.
.TP
.BR \-h , \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.PP
Durations accept any value understood by the Go standard library function
.BR time.ParseDuration (3),
such as
.BR 500ms ,
.BR 2s ,
or
.BR 1m30s .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command succeeded before the retry limit was reached.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed after exhausting all retries, or no command was provided.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B retry \-c 10 \-i 1s \-\- curl https://example.com/api
Retry the HTTP request up to 10 times, waiting one second between attempts.
.TP
.B retry \-t 10s \-\- make flaky-test
Retry running
.B make flaky-test
with a per-attempt timeout of 10 seconds.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timeout (1),
.BR watch (1)
